  message: "DONE — PR #58 merged, dev @ 85599923a3 (CI green; 9406 passed, all changed sources 100% cov).\n\nPREMISE-CHECK FIRST (3 confirmed, 1 WORSE than filed, 2 do NOT reproduce):\n\nCONFIRMED + FIXED:\n(1) 'ALL' wildcard unrecognized — node-http.yaml emits literal:ALL at 4 sites; openapi.py:362 knew only ANY and '*', so an ALL catch-all never linked where an equivalent ANY route would.\n(2) 'GET,POST' comma-joined list-artifact — framework_patterns.py:818 does ','.join on list-valued YAML method keys and only the route-materializer (framework_patterns.py:1921) splits it back, so the linker compared the joined string to a single verb: never equal, multi-method routes silently unlinked.\n(3) phantom '*' — confirmed ZERO producers.\n\nWORSE THAN FILED — the headline finding:\n(4a) 'MATCH' is NOT 'a lossy aggregate token that persists in http_method'. Live probe: Route::match(['get','post'], '/hybrid', ...) emitted NO route symbol and NO usage context — the entire route was ABSENT from the map. Root cause: php.py read the route path from args[0] unconditionally, but match's args[0] is the VERB ARRAY, so the string search failed and the call was skipped. An existing test (test_match_route_with_array_first_arg_skipped) PINNED this as expected behaviour ('currently skipped because first arg isn't a string') — a characterization test of the defect, now rewritten to the fixed contract.\n\nDO NOT REPRODUCE (recorded, not silently dropped):\n(4b) RESOURCE/API_RESOURCE 'double-representing' — live probe with the modern Controller::class form emits 7 real-verb route symbols (GET /photos, GET /photos/create, POST /photos, GET /photos/{id}, GET /photos/{id}/edit, PUT /photos/{id}, DELETE /photos/{id}). The RESOURCE aggregate survives ONLY on the call-site UsageContext, which honestly names the call that was made. Not a defect.\n(4c) Phoenix 'resources' collapsed to one token — live probe expands to all 7 routes (GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE). STALE.\n\nTHE FIX (chokepoint, not per-consumer patching): new routes.method_matches() + WILDCARD_HTTP_METHODS in the canonical route accessor — the module that already consolidated route_of/is_route. It understands the three shapes the verb field actually carries: absent (unconstrained), wildcard (ANY/ALL/*), comma-joined list. openapi.py now delegates instead of re-implementing a partial version. php.py shifts every positional argument by one for match (path args[1], controller args[2]) and emits the real verbs comma-joined — which composes with fix (2), so a recovered match route links to BOTH its GET and POST OpenAPI operations. A dynamically-built verb list (Route::match($verbs, ...)) falls back to the MATCH token rather than inventing verbs.\n\n'*' KEPT DELIBERATELY, not removed: it is the conventional HTTP wildcard spelling, costs one frozenset member, and removing it would narrow matching for any hand-authored route meta or future producer. Now documented in the vocabulary rather than left as an unexplained literal inside one consumer — the item's 'remove OR document' fork resolved as document.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: live probe before/after — Route::match now emits 'GET,POST /hybrid' with path=/hybrid and controller_action=FormController@handle (the offset shift verified on all three positional args). 12 new tests (method_matches semantics incl. wildcard-in-a-list and whitespace tolerance; openapi ALL + multi-method linking + a guard that the relaxation does NOT become a wildcard; php match recovery, dynamic-verb fallback, and empty/non-literal verb skipping). routes.py, openapi.py, php.py all at 100%.\n\nDEFERRED/NONE: no residual — the two non-reproducing defects are documented above rather than left open."  # e17e
